This fork (github.com/paleumm/Phantora, branch `cluster-sim`) modifies Phantora
upstream commit 301d9d9. The changes, used by github.com/paleumm/cluster-sim:

Simulator (phantora/)
  - Generic op timing: any outermost aten op the simulator does not model is
    keyed as TorchCallInfo::Generic {name, args} and timed from the perf DB
    (tests/perfdb/bench.py runs it via torch.ops.aten), instead of silently
    costing zero. View/metadata ops (NO_KERNEL_OPS) are skipped.
  - Dropped-op report: ops that still cannot be simulated are written to
    <perf-db>.dropped_ops.csv at exit.
  - Sender rank per flow: each flow of a collective carries its own sender's
    communicator rank; <timeline>.comms.json maps communicator ranks to host,
    process, device and global rank.
  - Step markers: PhantoraMarker(stream, tag) calls (phantora_mark in the C API,
    mark_step in tests/phantora_utils.py) recorded in the timeline.
  - NCCL collective latency: --nccl-base-latency-us / --nccl-hop-latency-us
    (base + steps x hop; default 0, i.e. upstream behaviour).
  - Timeline encoding fix: optional SDPA/Conv2d fields are no longer skipped by
    serde (bincode is not self-describing); perf-DB keys are unchanged.
  - Visualizer: no panic on NcclSend/NcclRecv; buffered JSON output.
  - Untimed-kernel report: kernels launched from outside PyTorch's own libraries
    (custom CUDA extensions via cudaLaunchKernel; Triton and other driver-API users
    via cuLaunchKernel/cuLaunchKernelEx) are reported once per launch and listed in
    <perf-db>.dropped_ops.csv as kernel:<library>:<kernel> (charged zero time, as
    before). The library is the kernel symbol's (runtime API) or the caller's
    (driver API), so PyTorch's own NVRTC kernels are not reported. Names in the CSV
    are quoted. The CUDA stub's cuModuleGetFunction returns named handles and the
    stub gains the driver calls Triton's launcher needs (cuLaunchKernelEx,
    cuFuncGet/SetAttribute, cuPointerGetAttribute(s), context calls), with H100-like
    values for the device attributes Triton reads.
  - Collective argument check: a rank joining a broadcast, all-reduce, all-gather or
    reduce-scatter with a count, datatype or root different from the first rank's
    stops the simulation with a message (sim.log and the ranks' stderr; ranks abort).
  - Equal-cost multipath (netsim): each flow takes one of the equal shortest paths
    (with 2+ spines: one spine), picked by a fixed hash of (seed, source, destination,
    size, count of earlier flows with the same three); upstream always took the first
    spine. Seed: `ecmp_seed` in [simulator], default 0. No smarter load balancing.

Tests and tools (tests/)
  - phantora_utils.py: mark_step(); optional skewed MoE routing for Megatron
    (PHANTORA_MOE_ROUTING=zipf:<s>).
  - phantora_utils.py: mark_step() also writes one line per step with the process's
    CPU time to $PHANTORA_STEP_LOG_DIR (nothing when unset); cluster-sim's
    cpu_time_per_step check reads it.
  - phantora_utils.py: gpt-oss experts are simulated with balanced top-k routing
    (each expert gets tokens x top_k / experts tokens), by default as a grouped-matmul
    expert layer; experts="hf_loop" reproduces stock transformers 4.56.2's per-expert
    training loop. Raises instead of computing every expert for every token.
  - test_megatron.py, test_deepspeed.py, test_torchtitan.py: step markers;
    test_megatron.py --moe_routing.
  - perfdb/bench.py: Generic op timing (schema-aligned arguments, crash-isolated
    worker, complex dtypes).
    Accuracy fixes (measured against real A100 runs): optional distinct operand
    buffers (PERFDB_ALIAS=0; upstream shares same-size operands, which made
    memory-bound multi-operand ops 30-50% too fast), 0-dim double/long operands
    of typed ops on the CPU (wrapped Python scalars), "f" floats as 2.0 (the
    norm order training uses); --merge keeps the DB manifest.
  - perfdb/{l40s,a100_40g,h100,h200,b200,b300}_v1: timing databases recorded
    with bench.py (FILLED.md lists entries taken from a sibling GPU).
  - perfdb/{l40s,a100_40g,h100,h200,b200,b300}_v2: the same key set re-recorded
    with the bench.py accuracy fixes (PERFDB_ALIAS=0); profiler-dropped kernels
    re-timed once, the rest listed in FILLED.md.

Dockerfile
  - pyarrow pinned to 19.0.1 (newer releases need NumPy 2; breaks TorchTitan).
